rthern Europe, member of the European Union since 1995, and an Arctic state.\\",\\n      \\"term_type\\": \\"place\\",\\n      \\"confidence\\": 1.0\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"canonical_term\\": \\"University of Oulu\\",\\n      \\"surface_forms\\": [\\"University of Oulu\\"],\\n      \\"negative_surface_forms\\": [],\\n      \\"canonical_description\\": \\"A public university located in Oulu, Finland, known for research in geography and Arctic studies.\\",\\n      \\"term_type\\": \\"entity\\",\\n      \\"confidence\\": 1.0\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"canonical_term\\": \\"Arctic futures\\",\\n      \\"surface_forms\\": [\\"Arctic futures\\"],\\n      \\"negative_surface_forms\\": [],\\n      \\"canonical_description\\": \\"Anticipated or projected developments and scenarios for the Arctic region, often related to economic, environmental, or geopolitical changes.\\",\\n      \\"term_type\\": \\"concept\\",\\n      \\"confidence\\": 0.85\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"canonical_term\\": \\"Shipping lanes\\",\\n      \\"surface_forms\\": [\\"shipping lanes\\"],\\n      \\"negative_surface_forms\\": [],\\n      \\"canonical_description\\": \\"Designated routes in the sea used by ships for navigation, particularly relevant in the Arctic due to melting sea ice.\\",\\n      \\"term_type\\": \\"concept\\",\\n      \\"confidence\\": 0.9\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"canonical_term\\": \\"Arctic states\\",\\n      \\"surface_forms\\": [\\"Arctic states\\"],\\n      \\"negative_surface_forms\\": [\\"non-Arctic states\\"],\\n      \\"canonical_description\\": \\"Countries with territory in the Arctic region, including both coastal and non-coastal states such as Finland, Sweden, and Iceland.\\",\\n      \\"term_type\\": \\"entity\\",\\n      \\"confidence\\": 1.0\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"canonical_term\\": \\"European Union\\",\\n      \\"surface_forms\\": [\\"EU\\", \\"European Union\\"],\\n      \\"negative_surface_forms\\": [],\\n      \\"canonical_description\\": \\"A polit