geopolitical significance.\\",\\n      \\"term_type\\": \\"place\\",\\n      \\"confidence\\": 0.97\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"canonical_term\\": \\"Russia’s Arctic strategy\\",\\n      \\"surface_forms\\": [\\"Russia’s Arctic strategy\\", \\"Russian Arctic strategy\\", \\"Russia's strategy in the Arctic\\"],\\n      \\"negative_surface_forms\\": [\\"US Arctic strategy\\", \\"Canadian Arctic strategy\\"],\\n      \\"canonical_description\\": \\"The set of policies and actions undertaken by Russia to secure its interests and presence in the Arctic region.\\",\\n      \\"term_type\\": \\"concept\\",\\n      \\"confidence\\": 0.95\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"canonical_term\\": \\"Dual-use capability\\",\\n      \\"surface_forms\\": [\\"dual-use capability\\", \\"dual-use capabilities\\", \\"dual use\\"],\\n      \\"negative_surface_forms\\": [\\"single-use\\", \\"civilian-only\\", \\"military-only\\"],\\n      \\"canonical_description\\": \\"The ability of a technology or asset to serve both civilian and military purposes.\\",\\n      \\"term_type\\": \\"concept\\",\\n      \\"confidence\\": 0.96\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"canonical_term\\": \\"Northern Sea Route\\",\\n      \\"surface_forms\\": [\\"Northern Sea Route\\", \\"NSR\\"],\\n      \\"negative_surface_forms\\": [\\"Northwest Passage\\", \\"Suez Canal\\"],\\n      \\"canonical_description\\": \\"A shipping lane along the Russian Arctic coast, connecting the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans, and a key route for Russian maritime strategy.\\",\\n      \\"term_type\\": \\"place\\",\\n      \\"confidence\\": 0.97\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"canonical_term\\": \\"Sanctions\\",\\n      \\"surface_forms\\": [\\"sanctions\\", \\"economic sanctions\\", \\"sanctions over it\\"],\\n      \\"negative_surface_forms\\": [\\"subsidies\\", \\"tariffs\\"],\\n      \\"canonical_description\\": \\"Restrictive measures imposed by one or more countries to influence the behavior or policies of another country, often affecting trade and