able of carrying cruise missiles and participating in joint patrols.\\",\\n      \\"term_type\\": \\"entity\\",\\n      \\"confidence\\": 1.0\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"canonical_term\\": \\"intercontinental ballistic missile\\",\\n      \\"surface_forms\\": [\\"intercontinental ballistic missile\\", \\"ICBM\\", \\"conventionally armed ICBM\\", \\"nuclear-armed ICBM\\"],\\n      \\"negative_surface_forms\\": [\\"cruise missile\\", \\"short-range ballistic missile\\"],\\n      \\"canonical_description\\": \\"A long-range missile capable of delivering nuclear or conventional warheads across continents.\\",\\n      \\"term_type\\": \\"entity\\",\\n      \\"confidence\\": 1.0\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"canonical_term\\": \\"hypersonic glide vehicle\\",\\n      \\"surface_forms\\": [\\"hypersonic glide vehicle\\", \\"HGV\\"],\\n      \\"negative_surface_forms\\": [\\"ballistic reentry vehicle\\"],\\n      \\"canonical_description\\": \\"A maneuverable warhead that travels at hypersonic speeds and can evade traditional missile defenses.\\",\\n      \\"term_type\\": \\"entity\\",\\n      \\"confidence\\": 1.0\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"canonical_term\\": \\"fractional orbital bombardment system\\",\\n      \\"surface_forms\\": [\\"fractional orbital bombardment system\\", \\"FOBS\\"],\\n      \\"negative_surface_forms\\": [\\"ICBM\\", \\"SLBM\\"],\\n      \\"canonical_description\\": \\"A missile system that places a warhead into low Earth orbit before de-orbiting it to strike a target, designed to evade early warning systems.\\",\\n      \\"term_type\\": \\"entity\\",\\n      \\"confidence\\": 1.0\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"canonical_term\\": \\"early warning radar\\",\\n      \\"surface_forms\\": [\\"early warning radar\\", \\"early warning system\\"],\\n      \\"negative_surface_forms\\": [\\"weather radar\\"],\\n      \\"canonical_description\\": \\"Radar systems designed to detect incoming missiles or aircraft at long range to provide advance notice of an attack.\