sing crystallization to produce solid products with speciﬁed properties. Chem. Ind.\n\n37.\n\n1997, 7, 488–500. (In Russian)\nJi, Z.; Yilmaz, B.; Warzywoda, J.; Sacco, A., Jr. Hydrothermal synthesis of titanosilicate ETS-10 using Ti(SO4)2.\nMicropor. Mezpor. Mat. 2005, 81, 1–10. [CrossRef]\n\n38. Motov, D.L. Physico-Chemistry and Sulphate Technology of Titanium-Rare Metal Raw Materials. Part 2; The Kola\n\nScience Center Press: Apatity, Russia, 2002. (In Russian)\n\n39. Gerasimova, L.G.; Nikolaev, A.I.; Kuz’mich, J.V.; Ivanyuk, G.Y.; Yakovenchuk, V.N.; Schukina, E.S.\nPatent RU-2539303: Method of Titanium-Silicon Sodium-Containing Composition Obtaining. U.S. Patent\nRU2539303C1, 20 January 2015.\n\n40. Gerasimova, L.G.; Maslova, M.V.; Nikolaev, A.I. Synthesis of new nano-porous titanosilicates using\n\nammonium oxysulphotitanite. J. Glass Phys. Chem. 2013, 39, 846–855. [CrossRef]\n\n© 2018 by the authors. Licensee MDPI, Basel, Switzerland. This article is an open access\narticle distributed under the terms and conditions of the Creative Commons Attribution\n(CC BY) license (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).\n\n417\n\n\f\fMDPI\n\nSt. Alban-Anlage 66\n\n4052 Basel\n\nSwitzerland\nTel. +41 61 683 77 34\n\nFax +41 61 302 89 18\n\nwww.mdpi.com\n\nMinerals Editorial Ofﬁce\nE-mail: minerals@mdpi.com\n\nwww.mdpi.com/journal/minerals\n\n\f\fMDPI\nSt. Alban-Anlage 66\n4052 Basel\nSwitzerland\n\nTel: +41 61 683 77 34\nFax: +41 61 302 89 18\n\nwww.mdpi.com\n\nISBN 978-3-03897-825-1\n\n\n	skipped	{"skipped_at": "2025-08-11T22:38:35.097Z", "skip_reason": "All 12 terms were duplicates of already-processed terms"}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	3a59766e020bfdde5be9d4090c553495a409c7b94a9488afa01e1ca16dfe6bab	\N	markitdown	gpt-4.1	tier_1	325842	1292856	{"routing_info":{"status":"tier_1","model":"gpt-4.1","estimated_tokens":325842,"limit":380000,"reason":"Content fits in Tier 1 model (gpt-4.1)","cost_tier":"standard"},"original_metadata":{"service":"Ingest::TokenAwareMarkitdownS