3, 289, 302–305, 308, 341\n\nStressors, 170, 241, 263, 273, 337, 345\nSustainability, 3–5, 11, 46, 48, 58, 153, 164,\n\n234, 239–240, 242, 244, 249, 252–257, 287,\n304, 337\n\nSustainable development, 136, 253–254\n\nT\nTourism, 18, 27, 30–31, 33, 35, 39, 46, 50, 56,\n64, 111, 177, 213, 240, 250, 266, 268,\n286–288, 291, 295–297, 299, 301,\n302–303, 305–308, 315, 339–340,\n342–343, 345\n\nTraditional foods/country foods/\n\nGreenlandic foods, 65–66, 68, 70, 73, 111,\n114, 117, 146, 172, 175, 177–178, 216, 264,\n267, 270–279, 344\n\nTraditional knowledge, 116–117, 168,\n\n171–172, 174–175, 178, 181–182, 208,\n276, 336, 340–341, 343\nTravel risks, 68–69, 205, 345\nTuktoyaktuk, 16, 17, 64–76, 198–199,\n\n337–339\n\nU\nUlukhaktok, 16, 17, 64–72, 75, 197,\n\n337–339\n\nUnja´ rga/Nesseby, 16, 217–219, 313–332,\n\n338–339\n\nUrban, 46, 74, 125–126, 140, 143, 147, 149,\n\n151, 153, 211, 240–241, 245–246,\n248–253, 255–258, 291, 294, 298, 321,\n337, 339, 345\n\n\fIndex\n\n353\n\nV\nVaranger, 217–218, 314–316, 319\nVestva˚ gøy, 16, 24, 31–33, 35–37, 39–40,\n\n225–230, 232–233, 240, 244, 248–249,\n251, 252, 253, 264, 272–273, 286, 289,\n293, 295, 297–298, 305\n\n43–51, 53–55, 57–58, 191–194, 338–340\n\nVulnerability, 63–77, 83–104, 107–127,\n\nWeather, downscaling, 32, 51, 327\nWellbeing, 2–3, 5, 8, 30, 39, 325, 336–337,\n\n131–159, 163–187, 222, 229, 234, 240,\n249–250, 254, 258–259, 263–281,\n285–309, 335–348\n\n340–341, 344–346\n\nWhitehorse, 16, 18, 210–211, 239–259,\n\n337–338, 340–341\n\nWinter thaw, 288–289, 291, 300, 303\n\nW\nWater, 18, 26, 28, 40, 43, 52, 57, 68, 71, 74,\n91, 94, 96, 98, 101, 108, 111, 113–115,\n118, 120, 122–125, 137, 143–146, 150, 154,\n157, 164, 167, 169–172, 177–178,\n180–181, 197–199, 202, 205–206,\n\nY\nYamalo-Nenets Autonomous Okrug, 17,\n\n83–84, 104, 200–201, 338\n\nYukon, 18, 239, 241, 243–253, 255,\n\n257, 338\n\n\n	skipped	{"skipped_at": "2025-08-11T22:38:35.098Z", "skip_reason": "All 17 terms were duplicates of already-processed terms"}	