ontier of national security. [极地安全：国家安全的新疆\n\n域], Guangming wang. https://news.gmw.cn/2021-04/25/content_34790839.htm\n\nFeng, H., & He, K. (2020). The study of Chinese scholars in foreign policy analysis: an emerging research\n\nprogram, The Pacific Review, 33(3–4), 362–385. DOI: https://doi.org/10.1080/09512748.2020.1738538\n\nFravel, T. M. (2017). China’s changing approach to military strategy: The science of military strategy from\n\n2001 to 2013. In McReynolds, J. (Eds.), China’s evolving military strategy (pp. 40–73). Washington, DC:\n\nThe Jamestown Foundation.\n\nFravel, T. M., Lavelle, K., & Odgaard, L. (2021). China engages the Arctic: a great power in a regime\n\ncomplex. Asian Security. DOI: https://doi.org/10.1080/14799855.2021.1986008\n\nGhoshal, D. (2020, February 14). China’s Submarine Fleet in the Arctic. European Security & Defence\n\nhttps://euro-sd.com/2020/02/articles/16137/chinas-submarine-fleet-in-the-arctic/\n\nGabuev, A. (2022, August 9). China’s new vassal. Foreign Affairs. https://www.foreignaffairs.com/china/\n\nchinas-new-vassal\n\nGhiselli, A. (2021). Protecting China’s interests overseas: Securitization and foreign policy. Oxford: Oxford\n\nUniversity Press. DOI: https://doi.org/10.1093/oso/9780198867395.001.0001\n\nGoldstein, L. J. (2019, June 1). Chinese nuclear armed submarines in Russian arctic ports? It could\n\nhappen. The National Interest. https://nationalinterest.org/feature/chinese-nuclear-armed-\n\nsubmarines-russian-arctic-ports-it-could-happen-60302\n\nGorbachev, M. (1987, October 1). Mikhail Gorbachev’s speech in Murmansk at the ceremonial meeting\n\non the occasion of the presentation of the Order of Lenin and the Gold Star Medal to the city of\n\nMurmansk. https://www.barentsinfo.fi/docs/gorbachev_speech.pdf\n\nGuarino, M., et al. (2020). Sea-ice-free Arctic during the last Interglacial supports fast future loss. Nature\n\nClimate Change, 10, 928–932. DOI: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41558-020-0865-2\n\nGuo, P., & Li, Z. (