n\nSakwa, Richard. 2008. “New ‘Cold War’ or Twenty Years Crisis?\nRussia and International Politics.” International Affairs 84, no. 2:\n241–67.\n\nSale, Richard, and Eugene Potapov. 2010. The Scramble for the Arctic:\nOwnership, Exploitation, and Conﬂict in the Far North. London: Frances\nLincoln.\n\nSergunin, Alexander, and Valery Konyshev. 2015. “Russia and the U.S.\nin the Arctic: A New Confrontation or Damage Limitation?” Valdai\nClub, September 21, at http://valdaiclub.com, accessed September 26,\n2015.\n\nSergunin, Alexander, and Valery Konyshev. 2014a. “Russia in Search of its\nArctic Strategy: Between Hard and Soft Power?” The Polar Journal 4,\nno. 1: 69–87.\n\nSergunin, Alexander, and Valery Konyshev. 2014b. “Four Dangerous\nMyths about Russia’s Plans for the Arctic.” Russia Direct, November\n25, at www.russia-direct.org/analysis/four-dangerous-myths-about-rus\nsias-plans-arctic, accessed July 3, 2015.\n\nShevtsova, Lilia. 2015. “Forward to the Past\n\nin Russia,” Journal of\n\nDemocracy 26, no. 2: 22–37.\n“4.4\n\nStaalesen, Atle.\n\n2015a.\n\nfor Russian Arctic\nDevelopment.” The Barents Observer, April 15, at http://barentsobser\nver.com/en/arctic/2015/04/eu44-billion-russian-arctic-development-15-\n04, accessed April 30, 2015.\n\nbillion Euros\n\nStaalesen, Atle. 2015b. “Expansionist Rogozin Looks to Arctic.” The Barents\nObserver, April 21, at http://barentsobserver.com/en/arctic/2015/04/expan\nsionist-rogozin-looks-arctic-21-04, accessed April 30, 2015.\n\nStaalesen, Atle. 2010. “Deal on Barents Sea Important for Europe.” (April\n27), at http://barentsobserver.com/en/sections/articles/deal-barents-sea-\nimportant-europe, accessed August 3, 2014.\n\nStier, Gabor. 2014. “Can ‘Putinism’ Compete as a Political System?”\n(September 10), at http://valdaiclub.com/russia_and_the_world/71784.\nhtml, accessed February 3, 2015.\n\nStoner, Kathryn, and Michael McFaul. 2015. “Who Lost Russia (This\nTime)? Vladimir Putin.” The Washington Quarterly 38, no. 2\n(Summer), at http://twq.elliott.gwu.edu/who-lost-russia-time-vladimir-\nputin, accessed August 27, 2015.\n\nSwart, Erik. 2016. “Defeat, Honor and the News: The Case of the Fall of\nBreda (1625) and the Dutch Republic.” European History Quarterly 46,\nno. 1: 6–26.\n\nTajfel, H. 1978. “The Psychological Structure of Intergroup Relations.”\nthe Social\nSocial Groups:\n\nDifferentiation between\nPsychology of Intergroup Relations. London: Academic.\n\nStudies\n\nin\n\n“The Development Strategy of the Arctic Zone of the Russian Federation.”\n2013 International Expert Council on Cooperation in the Arctic, April 14, at\nwww.iecca.ru/en/legislation/strategies/item/99-the-development-strategy-\nof-the-arctic-zone-of-the-russian-federation, accessed October 21, 2014.\nTrainor, Catherine. 2014. “Why Russia’s Arctic Strategy is Starting to\nWorry NATO.” Russia Direct, November 19, at www.russia-direct.\norg/why-russias-arctic-strategy-starting-worry-nato, accessed June 3,\n2015.\n\nTsygankov, Andrei P. 2014. “The Frustrating Partnership: Honor, Status,\nand Emotions in Russia’s Discourses of the West.” Communist and Post-\nCommunist Studies 47, no. 3–4:345–54.\n\n\fTszin’chzhoi, Chzhao, Ian Khai, Li Yunmin, and Liao Tao. 2014. “Kitai\na Shale\n\nrevoliutsiiu.”\n‘zapustil’\nRevolution). Oil & Gas Journal Russia, 12 (December): 58–64.\n\n‘Launches’\n\nslantsevuiu\n\n(China\n\n“Ukaz ‘O Strategii national’noi bezopasnosti Rossiiskoi Federatsii do 2020\ngoda’” (Decree “On the National Security Strategy of the Russian\nFederation to 2020”). 2009. The Kremlin, May 13, at http://kremlin.ru/\nevents/president/news/4047, accessed December 11, 2014.\n\n“Vladimir Putin predlozhil provesti Arkticheskiy subbotnik” (Vladimir\nPutin Proposes an Arctic Subbotnik). 2010. NTV, April 29, at www.\nntv.ru/novosti/191877/#ixzz22VGLrRJU, accessed July 3, 2014.\n“Vladimir Putin Signed Executive Order on the Polar Explorers’ Day.” The\nKremlin, May 21, at http://en.kremlin.ru/events/president/news/18145,\naccessed September 10, 2014.\n\n“Vstrecha s uchastnikami ekologicheskoi ekspeditsii na Arkhipelag Zemlia\nFrantsa-Iosifa” (Meeting with Ecological Expedition Participants on the\nFranz Josef Archipelago). 2012. President of Russia, July 30, at s.pre-\nzident.rf/novosti/16082, accessed September 14, 2014.\n\nPUTIN’S ARCTIC STRATEGY AFTER UKRAINE\n\n17\n\nWard, Steven. 2013. “Race, Status, and Japanese Revisionism in the Early\n\n1930s.” Security Studies 22, no. 4: 607–39.\n\nWood, Steve. 2013. “Prestige in World Politics: History, Theory,\n\nExpression.” International Politics, 50, no. 3: 387–411.\n\nWorking Group I. 2013. Contribution to the IPCC Fifth Assessment Report,\nClimate Change 2013: The Physical Science Basis. Summary for\nPolicymakers. Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change, at www.clima\ntechange2013.org/images/uploads/WGIAR5-SPM_Approved27Sep2013.\npdf, accessed May 3, 2015.\n\nWright, Robert. 1994. The Moral Animal: Evolutionary Psychology and\n\nEveryday Life. New York: Pantheon.\n\nZamyatina, Tamara. 2015. “US 2015 Military Strategy Adds Chill to New\nCold War Against Russia— Rogov.” TASS, July 2, at http://tass.ru/en/\nopinions/805511, accessed July 5, 2015.\n\nZamyatina, Tamara. 2014. “Russia Focuses Efforts on Expanding Presence\nin Arctic.” ITAR TASS, October 30, at en.itar-tass.com/opinions/1965,\naccessed October 31, 2014.\n\n\n	skipped	{"skipped_at": "2025-08-11T22:38:35.112Z", "skip_reason": "All 11 terms were duplicates of already-processed terms"}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	fbfff74daf1d914cef8d619c0416f3aa84eb84d1e280d9f54eac5668af5aeb5c	\N	markitdown	gpt-4.1	tier_1	25903	103401	{"routing_info":{"status":"tier_1","model":"gpt-4.1","estimated_tokens":25903,"limit":380000,"reason":"Content fits in Tier 1 model (gpt-4.1)","cost_tier":"standard"},"original_metadata":{"service":"Ingest::TokenAwareMarkitdownService","file_path":"/Volumes/jer4TBv3/enliterator/arctic_research/Putin's Arctic Strategy_Rotnem.pdf","file_size_bytes":754862,"content_length_