://www.rosatom.ru/journalist/news/\nobem-perevezennykh-gruzov-po-severnomu-morskomu-puti-v-2022-godu-sostavil-34-034\n-mln-tonn/.\n\n\fDEFENSE & SECURITY ANALYSIS\n\n429\n\n105. PortNews, ‘Inostrannyy tranzit po SMP udalos’ kompensirovat’ perevozkoy rossiyskikh\ngruzov v 2022 godu – Rosatom’, February 16, 2023, https://portnews.ru/news/343075/.\n106. LOGIRUS, ‘Dlya Sevmorputi stroyat miniﬂot iz 13 ledokolov’, December 1, 2021, https://\nlogirus.ru/news/transport/dlya_sevmorputi_stroyat_miniﬂot_iz_13_ledokolov.html.\n\n107. LOGIRUS, ‘Dlya Sevmorputi stroyat miniﬂot iz 13 ledokolov’.\n108. The Kremlin, ‘Soveshchaniye s chlenami Pravitel’stva’, May 17, 2023, http://kremlin.ru/\n\nevents/president/news/71146.\n\n109. Tat’yana Vil’de, ‘Vladimir Gutenev: obsuzhdayetsya sozdaniye otdel’noy gosprogrammy raz-\nvitiya dvigatelestroyeniya’, PortNews, May 16, 2023,https://portnews.ru/comments/3353/ .\n110. Vladimir Stanulevich, ‘“Atomﬂot”: Severnyy Ledovityy okean ne osvoboditsya oto l’da do\n2050 goda’, Regnum, November 26, 2021, https://regnum.ru/news/economy/3433963.html.\n111. Maria-Vittoria Guarino, Louise C. Sime, David Schröeder, Irene Malmierca-Vallet, Erica\nRosenblum, Mark Ringer, Jeﬀ Ridley, Danny Feltham, Cecilia Bitz, Eric J. Steig, Eric\nWolﬀ, Julienne Stroeve and Alistair Sellar, ‘Sea-Ice-Free Arctic during the Last Interglacial\nSupports Fast Future Loss’, Nature Climate Change 10 (2020): 928–32, https://www.nature.\ncom/articles/s41558-020-0865-2.\n\n112. The Northern Sea Route Administration, ‘Rules of Navigation in the Water Area of the\nNorthern Sea Route’, 2020, http://www.nsra.ru/en/oﬁtsialnaya_informatsiya/pravila_\nplavaniya.html.\n\n113. I.O. Dumanskaya, ‘Dependence of the Modern Icebreaker Fleet from Ice Conditions on the\n\nRussian Seas’, 15.\n\n114. Ibid., 21.\n115. INTERFAX, ‘“Rosatom” predlozhil izmenit’ pravila navigatsii po Sevmorputi iz-za noyabr’s-\n\nkogo krizisa’, December 22, 2021, https://www.interfax.ru/russia/811826.\n\n116. The Northern Sea Route Administration, ‘Object of Activity and Functions of NSRA’, 2023,\n\nhttp://www.nsra.ru/en/glavnaya/celi_funktsii.html.\n\n117. Ibid.\n118. Moe and Brigham, ‘Organization and Management Challenges’, 51.\n119. Ibid., p. 51.\n120. The Northern Sea Route Administration, ‘Rules of Navigation in the Water Area’.\n121. Ibid., 1–2.\n122. Ibid., 11.\n123. The Russian Government,\n\n‘Pravitel’stvo usovershenstvuyet sistemu upravleniya sudo-\nkhodstvom v akvatorii Severnogo morskogo puti. Postanovleniye ot 23 iyulya 2022 goda\n№1318, rasporyazheniye ot 23 iyulya 2022 goda №2019-r’,\nJuly 23, 2022, http://\ngovernment.ru/news/46152/.\n\n124. Skripnuk et al., ‘Analysis of the Current State of the Northern Sea Route’, 5.\n125. Vitaliy Chernov, ‘Russia’s Infrastructure Phantoms – 2021’, Port News, December 29, 2021,\n\nhttps://en.portnews.ru/comments/3104/.\n\nDisclosure statement\nNo potential conﬂict of interest was reported by the author(s).\n\nORCID\n\nNurlan Aliyev\n\nhttp://orcid.org/0000-0002-0522-4658\n\nNotes on contributor\nNurlan Aliyev is a lecturer in the University of Economics and Human Sciences in Warsaw. He is\nthe author of Reassessing Russia’s Security Policy.\n\n\n	skipped	{"skipped_at": "2025-08-11T22:38:35.114Z", "skip_reason": "All 15 terms were duplicates of already-processed terms"}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	9e92a1b093793d5cc09012b010a6457445e3875cf003ad9de33f27900cc8dbe5	\N	markitdown	gpt-4.1	tier_1	21960	87328	{"routing_info":{"status":"tier_1","model":"gpt-4.1","estimated_tokens":21960,"limit":380000,"reason":"Content fits in Tier 1 model (gpt-4.1)","cost_tier":"standard"},"original_metadata":{"service":"Ingest::TokenAwareMarkitdownService","file_path":"/Volumes/jer4TBv3/enliterator/arctic_research/Russia's Arctic icebreaking capability-an assessment_Aliyev.pdf","file_size_bytes":2125910,"content_length_chars":87328,"estimated_tokens":21960,"timestamp":"2025-08-11T22:07:53Z","supported_formats":[".pdf",".docx",".pptx",".xlsx",".md",".txt",".htm