n and Refugee Protection Act, s.\n118.\n\n33  Criminal Code of Canada, s. 279.03(1).\n34  Public Law 106-386 [H.R. 3244].\n35  22 USC § 7102.\n36  22 USC § 7102(8).\n37  8 US Code § 1182 (2)(H)(i), (ii).\n38  18 US Code § 1543.\n39  Order No. 909, as amended by Act Nos.\n\n‘Trump Vows to Fight “Epidemic” of\nHuman Trafficking’, Associated Press News,\n23 February 2017. But see ‘Trump\nAdministration’s Talk on Human\nTrafficking Must Be Matched By Deeds’,\nCNN, 1 July 2017.\n\n48  US Department of Justice, National\n\nStrategy to Combat Human Trafficking\n(Washington, DC: US Government,\n2017).\n\n49  The US National Strategy focuses\n\nextensively on actions and approaches to\ncombat human trafficking undertaken by\nits Human Trafficking Prosecution Unit,\nthe US Attorneys’ Offices, the Federal\nBureau of Investigation, Department of\nJustice: US Department of Justice,\nNational Strategy.\n\n50  US Department of Justice, National\n\nStrategy, Introduction.\n\n51  US Department of Justice, National\n\nStrategy, 3.\n\n52  Joint Statement of the United States-Nordic\nLeaders Summit, Washington, DC, 13 May\n2016, 5.\n\n53  Ministry for Children, Gender Equality,\n\nIntegration and Social Affairs, Action Plan\nto Combat Trafficking in Human Beings\n2015–2018 (Copenhagen: Skabertrang,\n2015).\n\n1389 and 1400 (2005).\n\n54  Danish Centre Against Human Trafficking,\n\n40  Directive 2011/36/EU of the European\nParliament and of the Council of 5 April\n2011 on preventing and combating\ntrafficking in human beings and protecting\nits victims, and replacing Council\nFramework Decision 2002/629/JHA.\n\n41  Consolidation Act, No. 945 (2006).\n42\n\nInternational Organization for Migration,\nCountry Office in Denmark, ‘Counter-\nTrafficking’, https://denmark.iom.int/\ncounter-trafficking.\n\n43  Department of Public Safety, National\n\nAction Plan to Combat Human Trafficking,\n(Ottawa: Government of Canada, 2012).\n\n44  Department of Public Safety, National\n\nAction Plan, 11, 1